  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GZ - IDF Public Procurement  Reform Supp</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose or objective of the IDF grant is to assist the PA in implementing top priority procurement reform recommendations as a result of the CPAR exercise.  To assist the Palestinian Authority in implementing Public procurement reform in line with the Country Procurement Assessment Report recommendations. The Activities for which the Grant is given are as follows: (a) For the ppurpose of formulating a uniform procurement law: (i) the identifying of key facets of existiong procurement laws, including involving stakeholders; (ii) the carrying out of workshops to document key issues and resolutions; and (iii) the drafting of a unified public procurement law and relevant regulations; (b) provision of technical assisatance for the purposes of developing standard national bidding documents for procurement of works, goods and services; and (c) capacity building of key Palestinian Authority staff, including staff from Non Governmental Organizations and private sector in carrying out public procurement activities.</narrative>
  </description>
